The boundary with the internet: exits, NAT and port forwards

Usage:
  olr gateway [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add an exit or a port forward
  disable     Remove routing policy and port forwards, keeping them configured
  enable      Apply routing policy and port forwards
  rm          Remove an exit, a port forward, or a network's assignment
  set         Change an exit assignment or a port forward
  show        Show exits, port forwards, and which networks use what
  status      Show each exit's health, what uses it, and drift

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for gateway

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")

Use "olr gateway [command] --help" for more information about a command.
